
---
import DocsLayout from '/src/layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import DocsCode from '/src/components/DocsCode.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Lua & LSL Docs">
<div class="dashboard summary-function">
  <div class="dashboard-header">
    <span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll.GroundNormal(Offset: vector): vector`} lang="slua" /></span>
    <span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`vector llGroundNormal(vector Offset);`} lang="lsl" /></span>
  </div>

  <div class="dashboard-body">
    <div class="dash-col">
      <p>  <p>Returns a vector that is the ground [](https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/File:Wikipedia-16px.png)&#8201;<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Normal_(geometry" target="_blank">normal</a>) from the current <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlGetPos" target="_blank">position</a> + <b>offset</b>.</p>
</p>
      <table class="param-table" id="parameters">
        <tr>
          <td><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>vector</span></td>
          <td><span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span>vector</span></td>
          <td>Offset / <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Category:LSL_Parameters/offset" target="_blank">offset</a></td>
          <td>offset relative to the prim's position and expressed in <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Viewer_coordinate_frames#Local" target="_blank">local coordinates</a></td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Categories</div>
      <ul class="meta-list">
        <li>region</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Tech Specs</div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">Energy</span><span class="tech-val">10</span></div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">LSO ID</span><span class="tech-val">222</span></div>

      <div class="label-stack">
        <span class="attr-label bg-mandatory">Use Return</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
  <p>The requested position needs to be in the same region.</p>
  <p>Only the <b>x</b> and <b>y</b> coordinates in <b>offset</b> are important, the <b>z</b> component is ignored.</p>
  <h2>Specification</h2>
  <p>This function is defined as:</p>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`vector llGroundNormal(vector offset)
{
    vector slope = llGroundSlope(offset);
    return <slope.x, slope.y, 1.0>;
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>There seems to some confusion be between a <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Normal_%28geometry%29" target="_blank">Surface Normal</a> (the direction from the surface) and <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unit_vector" target="_blank">Normalized Vector</a> (a vector with a magnitude of 1.0, AKA Unit Vector). This function does <b>not</b> return a unit vector. Surface normals may encode additional information in the magnitude of the vector. If you need a Unit Vector, simply use <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlVecNorm" target="_blank">llVecNorm</a>.</li>
  </ul>
